  MT=456 Number of prompt neutrons per fission                    9637 1451   53
    The experimental data of 2.75+-0.08 measured by Zhuravlev et  9637 1451   54
    al./6/ seems to be too small. A value of 3.00 at 0 eV         9637 1451   55
    was assumed. An energy dependent term was based on the        9637 1451   56
    systematics derived by Ohsawa/7/.                             9637 1451   57
                                                                  9637 1451   58
  MT=458 Components of energy release due to fission              9637 1451   59
    Total energy and prompt energy were calculated from mass      9637 1451   60
    balance using JENDL-4 fission yields data and mass excess     9637 1451   61
    evaluation. Mass excess values were from Audi's 2009          9637 1451   62
    evaluation/8/. Delayed energy values were calculated from     9637 1451   63
    the energy release for infinite irradiation using JENDL FP    9637 1451   64
    Decay Data File 2000 and JENDL-4 yields data. For delayed     9637 1451   65
    neutron energy, as the JENDL FP Decay Data File 2000/9/ does  9637 1451   66
    not include average neutron energy values, the average values 9637 1451   67
    were calculated using the formula shown in the report by      9637 1451   68
    T.R. England/10/. The fractions of prompt energy were         9637 1451   69
    calculated using the fractions of Sher's evaluation/11/ when  9637 1451   70
    they were provided. When the fractions were not given by Sher,9637 1451   71
    averaged fractions were used.                                 9637 1451   72
