  Calculation with CCONE code                                     9637 1451  258
***************************************************************** 9637 1451  259
                                                                  9637 1451  260
  Models and parameters used in the CCONE/2/ calculation          9637 1451  261
  1) Coupled channel optical model                                9637 1451  262
     Levels in the rotational band were included. Optical model   9637 1451  263
     potential and coupled levels are shown in Table 1.           9637 1451  264
                                                                  9637 1451  265
  2) Two-component exciton model/29/                              9637 1451  266
    * Global parametrization of Koning-Duijvestijn/30/            9637 1451  267
      was used.                                                   9637 1451  268
    * Gamma emission channel/31/ was added to simulate direct     9637 1451  269
      and semi-direct capture reaction.                           9637 1451  270
                                                                  9637 1451  271
  3) Hauser-Feshbach statistical model                            9637 1451  272
    * Moldauer width fluctuation correction/32/ was included.     9637 1451  273
    * Neutron, gamma and fission decay channel were included.     9637 1451  274
    * Transmission coefficients of neutrons were taken from       9637 1451  275
      coupled channel calculation in Table 1.                     9637 1451  276
    * The level scheme of the target is shown in Table 2.         9637 1451  277
    * Level density formula of constant temperature and Fermi-gas 9637 1451  278
      model were used with shell energy correction and collective 9637 1451  279
      enhancement factor. Parameters are shown in Table 3.        9637 1451  280
    * Fission channel:                                            9637 1451  281
      Double humped fission barriers were assumed.                9637 1451  282
      Fission barrier penetrabilities were calculated with        9637 1451  283
      Hill-Wheler formula/33/. Fission barrier parameters were    9637 1451  284
      shown in Table 4. Transition state model was used and       9637 1451  285
      continuum levels are assumed above the saddles. The level   9637 1451  286
      density parameters for inner and outer saddles are shown in 9637 1451  287
      Tables 5 and 6, respectively.                               9637 1451  288
    * Gamma-ray strength function of Kopecky et al/34/,/35/       9637 1451  289
      was used. The prameters are shown in Table 7.               9637 1451  290
